Chapter: RecordEqualityVector

 The arm for the vector-field half of record and variant equality.

 A `Vector n T` field answers `==` with a `VectorMask n`, and the fold that
 turns a mask into a Boolean is declared at arity 2, so nothing in the language
 compares a vector wider than 2 today, and ec-extract is bound the same way. The desugarer therefore synthesises NO
 equality helper for a type carrying such a field, and this file pins the
 consequence that matters: the unit COMPILES. Before that guard, a record with
 a vector field failed with CDX2001 on a span nobody wrote, whether or not
 anything ever compared it.

 What this file deliberately does NOT pin is whether two structurally equal
 values with vector fields answer True: they do not, because such a type falls
 back to pointer comparison the way every record did before record bodies were
 widened into the gate. That is COMPILER-77, and pinning today's answer here
 would make its fix look like a regression.

Section: Types

  Later = record { n : Integer }

  Holder = record { item : Later, vec : SizedVec 4 Integer }

  Shape =
    | Empty
    | Lane (SizedVec 4 Integer)

Section: Body

  v4 : Integer -> SizedVec 4 Integer
  v4 (n) = vec-cons 4 (vec-cons 3 (vec-cons 2 (vec-singleton n)))

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let a = Holder { item = Later { n = 1 }, vec = v4 7 }
    in let s = Lane (v4 7)
    in act
     print-line-uni ("record-self=" & show (a == a))
     print-line-uni ("variant-self=" & show (s == s))
    end
  end

